WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.867
Poor detections create unnecessary workload and may erode trust in monitoring systems.

00:00:04.867 --> 00:00:09.238
If analysts repeatedly see alerts that are vague, irrelevant, or unactionable,

00:00:09.238 --> 00:00:11.621
they may learn to discount them.

00:00:11.621 --> 00:00:14.005
High-quality detections balance sensitivity with specificity.

00:00:14.005 --> 00:00:15.992
Sensitivity helps identify suspicious behavior,

00:00:15.992 --> 00:00:21.951
while specificity helps reduce unnecessary noise by focusing on events that match the intended condition.

00:00:21.951 --> 00:00:25.924
Detection engineers should consider whether alerts are understandable, actionable, relevant,

00:00:25.924 --> 00:00:26.718
and maintainable.

00:00:26.718 --> 00:00:31.883
The output should explain what happened, why it matters, what entity was involved,

00:00:31.883 --> 00:00:33.869
and what context supports investigation.

00:00:33.869 --> 00:00:38.240
Reducing false positives improves analyst efficiency and supports better defensive outcomes.

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:40.623
The goal is not silent systems;

00:00:40.623 --> 00:00:46.980
the goal is a signal stream that earns trust because it helps people act with confidence.
